From c5b03638c4ceb843c92578d69392db5bb19b70f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:18:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Add the surface-effect correction (REDCAPP, DReaMIT) and
 its calibration

TopoSCALE takes air temperature from the pressure levels: free-atmosphere
air, without the inversions, cold-air pools and daily cycle that ERA5
resolves at its surface. The option toposcale.surface_effect adds back a
terrain-weighted share of the ERA5 surface signal dT = t2m - T_pl(z_grid):
T = T_pl + w dT + beta(t), the same for the dew point (capped at T), and
the longwave uses the corrected values. Off by default: outputs unchanged.

- surface_effect.py: hypsometric position, relief and MRVBF on a context
  DEM, the REDCAPP (Cao et al. 2017) and DReaMIT (Pozsgay et al. 2026)
  weights with their published coefficients, coefficients files, setup
  for the downscaler.
- surface_calib.py: station loaders (MeteoSwiss, generic csv), pairing
  with a run made with the diagnostics, per-station weights, pooled fit,
  cross-validation (by station or time block), bootstrap, YAML output.
- toposcale_core / topo_scale_zarr / topoclass: the correction and the
  diagnostics t_pl, dT_surf, dTd_surf.
- Synthetic tests: off unchanged, limits, humidity bounds, indices on
  synthetic DEMs, parameter recovery, downscaler integration.

